# Installation and Build Guide

## 1. Obtain the Artifact

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Auguuust/K2O.git
cd K2O
```

The repository contains three independently buildable methods:

| Method | Source directory |
|---|---|
| K2O | `K2O/` |
| GoogleLI | `Baselines/rocksdb-google/` |
| LeaderKV | `Baselines/rocksdb-leader/` |

In the commands below, replace `/path/to/<method>` with one of these
directories.

## 2. Install Dependencies

See `REQUIREMENTS` for the complete environment description. On Ubuntu:

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y build-essential cmake python3 \
  zlib1g-dev libsnappy-dev liblz4-dev libzstd-dev \
  libgflags-dev libbz2-dev
```

## 3. Configure and Compile

```bash
cd /path/to/<method>
mkdir -p build
cd build
cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..
make db_bench -j"$(nproc)"
```

A successful build produces:

```text
/path/to/<method>/build/db_bench
```

To rebuild after changing configuration:

```bash
cd /path/to/<method>/build
rm -f CMakeCache.txt
rm -rf CMakeFiles
cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..
make db_bench -j"$(nproc)"
```

## 4. Run a K2O Smoke Test

The following reduced-size command checks that the K2O executable can create a
database and complete point reads. Change the database path if `/tmp` is not
suitable.

```bash
cd /path/to/K2O/build
./db_bench \
  --db=/tmp/k2o-smoke-db \
  --benchmarks=fillrandom,readrandom \
  --num=100000 \
  --reads=100000 \
  --key_size=24 \
  --value_size=128 \
  --compression_type=None \
  --use_learned_index=true
```

Successful execution prints separate `fillrandom` and `readrandom` result
lines containing latency and operations per second.

## 5. Configure Full Experiments

Before running full experiments, set the following paths to locations valid on
the evaluation machine:

- `DB_PATH`: database directory;
- `WORKLOAD_PATH`: YCSB or dataset-specific workload directory;
- `EXP_ROOT`: experiment output directory.

The default experiment scale used by the artifact is:

- 64,000,000 load or fill operations;
- 10,000,000 run or read operations;
- 24-byte keys;
- 128-byte values unless another value size is selected.

Benchmark helper scripts are included in the implementation directories where
provided. Review their configuration block before execution. The scripts may
delete the configured database directory and clear the Linux page cache.

## 6. Run a Configured Helper Script

From a method directory containing `build/test.py`:

```bash
cd /path/to/<method>
python3 ./build/test.py
```

The experiment loops in `main()` are disabled by default. Enable only the
specific random, YCSB, or dataset workload calls required for the evaluation.

## 7. Locate Results

Results are written under the configured `EXP_ROOT`. Depending on the
selected test, outputs include the full log, extracted IOPS, trace statistics,
and per-operation I/O-count JSON files. See `STATUS` and `README.md` for
the expected filenames.
